  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** AdvanSix is navigating a protracted cyclical downturn in nylon, where a “lower-for-longer” environment persists. While sales grew, profitability was squeezed by steeply higher sulfur and natural gas costs and the lap of one-time insurance benefits, creating a sharp divergence between top-line strength and margin erosion. On the positive side, rising regional demand for diesel exhaust fluid (DEF) presents a promising growth avenue for its ammonia platform, hinting at diversifying end-market dynamics.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is actively adapting, evaluating an expansion of the integrated ammonia platform to capitalize on DEF demand and appointing a new CFO to refresh the executive team. Although quarterly earnings fell short of expectations, the revenue beat suggests underlying operational steadiness. The strategic pivot toward ammonia growth and organizational renewal signals a deliberate effort to steer through the cycle, though near-term credibility will hinge on arresting margin deterioration.",
